sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-second-assessor-audit-v3-bressloff-v1-form-constants-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — Parameter expressivity: 76/100" ;
        rdfs:comment "The script provides parameter_sweep and a --sweep CLI flag covering six biophysical coupling parameters (lateral_wide_sigma, lateral_inhibition, lateral_spread_deg, lateral_sigma, eigen_beta, local_sigma_deg) and plots three sweeps in Panels F and G. Increasing lateral_wide_sigma from 1.5 to 6.0 monotonically lowers q* from 1.46 to 0.70, increasing lateral_inhibition from 0 to 1 monotonically raises q* from the 0.05 floor to 1.00, and sweeping lateral_spread_deg from 0 to 90 degrees induces two parity flips between odd and even branches at 45 and 90 degrees. However, all five gallery columns share the exact same biophysical coupling parameters (lateral_sigma=1.0, lateral_wide_sigma=1.5, lateral_inhibition=1.0, lateral_spread_deg=60.0, eigen_beta=0.35, giving identical q* = 1.447468 and 11 cycles) and differ solely via manual preset overrides of pattern and pattern_angle_deg (-12 pts). Moreover, across all six sweepable parameters, the unrestricted cubic branch selection remains locked to rhombic (roll_ever_stable=False and square_ever_stable=False everywhere), so sweeping the model's coupling parameters never drives transitions across Klüver's form- constant families (-8 pts). Finally, the lateral_spread_deg sweep in Panel G evaluates q* on a 128-point grid (step 0.0272) over which q* takes only three discrete values between 0.9465 and 1.0280, yielding a quantized step curve (-4 pts). Evidence: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L380–L460: Gallery presets in PAPER_PRESETS share identical coupling parameters and vary only pattern, pattern_angle_deg, and sharpness <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L380-L460>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L1506–L1560: SWEEPABLE_PARAMS and parameter_sweep implementation over 6 coupling parameters <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L1506-L1560>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L1687–L1707: Sweep summaries confirming unrestricted_selected_family is solely rhombic and roll_ever_stable / square_ever_stable are always False <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L1687-L1707>; bressloff_v1_metrics.csv L31–L43: CSV kluver_form_constant and parameter_sweep rows showing identical critical_q=1.447468 across all 5 gallery presets and 3-bin quantization in lateral_spread_deg <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/bressloff_v1_metrics.csv#L31-L43>." ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-parameter-expressivity> ;
        pk:hasProbability "0.76"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-parameter-expressivity> rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants (2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py, docs/media/bressloff_v1_form_constants.gif, bressloff_v1_metrics.csv, datasets/bressloff/horton_hoyt_1991_magnification.json) satisfies the MorphoEval 0.1.0 criterion 'Parameter expressivity' for Homo sapiens primary visual cortex (V1) — geometric visual hallucinations (Klüver form constants) and flicker phosphenes" ;
        dcterms:identifier "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Gemini 4 Argon (Cursor agent, blinded second assessor)" .
}

